-If it converges quickly, then that means you started very close to the true value
-This sinusoidal function will return in a practicum, so get familiar with it

-Chi^2 assumes Gaussian statistics
-If chi^2 >> 1, you made a poor measurment or something else is incorrect; chi^2 << 1 means we probably have a misunderstanding of the experiment
-expectation value for chi^2 = v, where v is the degrees of freedom, in most cases 1

